@@ -1,3 +1,9 @@
+# poll-until — sleep between checks; act only when state calls for it; exit on a state predicate.
+# Poll a deploy's status endpoint on a timer. If it comes back red, let a coding agent push a
+# fix; if it's still pending, sleep and check again. The exit condition reads the HTTP response
+# (status == green), never the agent's own claim — use this pattern when the thing you're
+# waiting on has its own external status that changes on its own schedule (deploys, long jobs,
+# infra provisioning), not for work an agent can just finish in one pass.
